---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Turf Tips" description="Installation, watering, and maintenance guidance for new sod in North Texas heat.">
  <section class="ph"><div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Turf Tips</span>
    <h1>Get your new sod through the first 30 days.</h1>
    <p class="lede">What happens in the first month decides whether the lawn roots in or struggles all season. Here is what matters most.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section><div class="wrap grid g2">
    <div class="card"><h3>Lay it fast</h3><p>Sod is a living, perishable product. Install the day it arrives. Pallets left sitting in summer heat will heat up from the inside and decline quickly.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Tight seams</h3><p>Butt the pieces together with no gaps. Open seams dry out at the edges and invite weeds before the lawn knits together.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Water immediately</h3><p>Start watering as soon as a section is safely laid — do not wait for the whole yard to finish. Root contact and moisture matter more than anything else in week one.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Deep, then less often</h3><p>Frequent shallow watering the first two weeks. Once rooted, shift to deeper and less frequent so roots chase moisture downward.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Stay off it</h3><p>Keep traffic light until the sod knits down. Tug a corner — if it resists, it is rooting.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Sharp blades, no scalping</h3><p>First mow once rooted. Sharp blades, and never remove more than a third of the blade height at once.</p></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section-alt"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center">
    <h2>Questions about your specific yard?</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="margin:0 auto 28px">Sun, slope, soil, and irrigation all change the answer. Ask us.</p>
    <a href="/contact" class="btn">Contact Us</a>
  </div></section>
</Base>
<style>.ph{background:linear-gradient(135deg,#24462c,#0f1f12);padding:clamp(60px,9vw,120px) 0}</style>
